## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to implement a branchless, correct popcount in O(1) time, a common low-level optimization in performance-critical code (DBs, networking) at senior-level shops like Oracle and Twitter.

## Key Concepts
- Branchless bit counting
- Parallel bit manipulation with masks
- 32-bit mask progression and final accumulation

## Code Example
```c
uint32_t popcount32(uint32_t x){
  x = x - ((x >> 1) & 0x55555555);
  x = (x & 0x33333333) + ((x >> 2) & 0x33333333);
  x = (x + (x >> 4)) & 0x0F0F0F0F;
  x = x + (x >> 8);
  x = x + (x >> 16);
  return x & 0x3F;
}
```

